Translation patch: the flags types `MariadbCapabilities`, `StmtBulkExecuteFlags`, `BinlogDumpFlags`

Change: These three `my_bitflags!` invocations become `my_plain_bitflags!` (the macro of patch 20), and drop `Debug` from their `derive` list (the macro writes the `bitflags` one).
Why: As for patch 20: `bitflags!` goes through the external `bitflags::Bits`/`Flags` traits, which Aeneas has no model for. The handshake, SSL request, bulk-execute and binlog-dump packets store these types.
Behaviour: Identical, for the reasons given in patch 20 (the macro writes out the `bitflags` 2.13 API with the same bodies, constants, `Debug` output and derived impls).

